Refactoring Evidence:

1 - Created Design Tokens
* Before I created Design Tokens:
COlors were fixed to hex codes and thrown into individual classes
however, the design tokens now make up for uniform global color changes.
* After I created Design Tokens:
All use of color in my CSS are now recurring. Typography is also fixed, and scaling is done uniformly. Shape values are also reusable.
* Impact:
This will reduce style duplication and ensure that applying color will only require a single variable! This helps prevent errors and modifying every individual class.

2 - Component Modularization
* Before I added Component Modularization
Styles for complex layouts and repeating components were written for specific pages, which bloats my files with code and duplicates.
* After I added Component Modularization
Recurring UI elements are now self contained and in modular components that can be reused across the site. Like lego pieces.
* Impact: This improves code readability, and maintaining the site. Components can now be plugged in directly and built upon like lego pieces.